From: AdobeWine
Subject: [PATCH] Functions Adobe's apps import that Wine lacks: implement or forward them.

From a scan of every binary in the Adobe install folders (5664 files) against Wine's exports (docs/DLL-MAP.md).
Calling a missing import aborts the process, so a rarely used path could take an app down.
Real: RegOpenKeyTransacted, RegDeleteKeyTransacted (no transaction, as Wine has none), CreateFileMappingNumaA,
MFCreateMediaBufferWrapper, VariantCompare, spoolss printer calls and NetWkstaGetInfo (forwards), the *64 marshaling
names (forwards to the plain ones). Report an honest "nothing here" (no packages, no pointer devices, no private
namespaces, no enclaves): the rest of the kernel32/kernelbase, user32, powrprof, userenv and wininet entries.
Test: wine/tests/gapmap.

---
